  max |CVaR[unserved]_aware - CVaR[unserved]_neutral| = 1.705e-13 MW   on a base of 418.94 MW  (relative 4.07e-16)
  -> unserved energy is INVARIANT to the day-ahead policy
  share of tail cost that is unreachable (unserved x VOLL): 82.8%
  reachable tail cost (energy + deviations): 80605.6 of 471364.3

  Read this as the ceiling: a gap quoted as X% of tail cost is
  5.80x that as a share of the cost the policy can actually move.

==============================================================================
W1  Paired headline, 15 seeds, eps=0.3, beta=0.99
==============================================================================
Differences are paired on the seed, so instance-to-instance variance
cancels. Both comparisons are reported: against the risk-neutral
stochastic planner (the honest one) and against the deterministic
policy (easier, but it never sees the scenario set).
